    "notes": "Q1128327/relation3370923 identifies El Castillo. Standard pinned PMTiles building52776561504171 and173 component records retain the actual compound/stair outline, nine stage controls,89 mapped tread levels and summit landings, summit walls/roof and north terminal parts. The internal east axis is24.02 degrees south of east; the north stair and three-opening summit facade face toward local-Z negative. Raw east/south coordinates preserve signed orientation without using the older undirected map axis. Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged 161-square/6m standard DEM. Raw east/south coordinates retain the internal24.02-degree grid, north stair and serpent terminals. The north approach fixes the grade6.194m above the raw reference datum. The exact occupied footprint, including the serpent foundations, has an opaque floor and sampled edge joins at every level. Only this occupied floor opens terrain; a separate guarded convex replacement envelope was checked against every independent map building. Full-site loading removes all174 pyramid/component records and preserves54 independent tile buildings exactly. Three native water features retain5311.744209402124 square metres. Failure keeps all228 native tile buildings and original ground. Eviction restores both surfaces and frees model geometry. Synthetic64m partial residency retains safe failure/eviction behavior but exposes the known renderer sky gaps at temporary clipped floor/terrain boundaries. This limitation remains pending and is not a passed partial-contact condition. DEM/canopy levels and exposed edge foundations are approximate visualization fits, not archaeological survey levels.",
    "groundContactBasis": "Reviewed approximate full-site fit on the unchanged 161-square/6m standard DEM. Raw east/south coordinates retain the internal24.02-degree grid, north stair and serpent terminals. The north approach fixes the grade6.194m above the raw reference datum. The exact occupied footprint, including the serpent foundations, has an opaque floor and sampled edge joins at every level. Only this occupied floor opens terrain; a separate guarded convex replacement envelope was checked against every independent map building. Full-site loading removes all174 pyramid/component records and preserves54 independent tile buildings exactly. Three native water features retain5311.744209402124 square metres. Failure keeps all228 native tile buildings and original ground. Eviction restores both surfaces and frees model geometry. Synthetic64m partial residency retains safe failure/eviction behavior but exposes the known renderer sky gaps at temporary clipped floor/terrain boundaries. This limitation remains pending and is not a passed partial-contact condition. DEM/canopy levels and exposed edge foundations are approximate visualization fits, not archaeological survey levels."
  },
